A||||3||Fiero_Freak||Pulling motor...||||1||
Z||000000||Fiero_Freak||12-29-2000||10:29 PM||||So what's the best procedure for pulling the car off the cradle.  I have a engine hoist.  Didn't know where's a good place to attach it to the car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||12-30-2000||12:04 AM||||A guy near me usually catches hooks in the tops of the shock towers. Lifts the car with a come-a-long, connected to a beam in his garage.<P>What I'd like to know is how much weight you're lifting, when you lift the car up off of the cradle. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Max The Chainsaw||12-30-2000||06:26 AM||||Must not be a lot of weight, a mechanic I know who used to work for a Pontiac dealer in the 80's said they used to block up the cradle and two guys, one on each corner, would lift the body off the cradle and walk it forward.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-30-2000||01:51 PM||||Well.... a fiero unloaded weight is about 2400#. (GVW includes max cargo and passenger loads.)<P>Figure you have 600-700# sitting on the floor. you're under a ton now. <P>A big chunk of weight is on the front end.<P>I figure your about 800-1000 pounds on the hook. Not real heavy but more than 2 of most people could lift. 4 people in decent shape could be able to handle it safely. Trick is finding solid grab points. Get ahold of it the wrong way and it could come crashing down.<P>I wouldn't hook directly to the towers myself. Just to avoid marking up the hardware if nothing else. I'd cut a couple chunks of steel long enough to sit inside the top of the tower and chain to them. That way the load is spread a bit. A couple sections of 3/4 inch steel pipe would work.<P>Some people hook to the trunk latch ring. I'm not real hot on that idea. Normally the ring is pretty solid. If the ring area is rusted and you don't know it you could have it pull off. Worse it could time bomb you after it's been in the air awhile.||||reg||1
